Simple LED Circuit Using a Resistor


Aim


To construct a basic LED circuit using a current-limiting resistor.


Components Required




LED


330-ohm resistor


5 V DC supply


Connecting wires




Working Principle


The LED emits light when current flows through it in the forward direction. The resistor limits the current and protects the LED from excessive current.


Applications




Indicator lights


Electronic devices


Status indicators




Advantages




Simple circuit


Low cost


Easy to understand


Requires few components




Conclusion


This project demonstrates the basic principles of current limiting and LED operation in an electronic circuit.

